<title>GERMANY: West German Nov industry orders rise 0.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>West German Nov industry orders rise 0.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY ORDERS     Nov 96     Oct 96     Nov 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)   +0.2	 +3.2(3.4)  +2.0</p>
<p> Year-on-year			+5.5	 +7.4(7.5)   n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		 97.7	 97.5(97.6)  92.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted, provisional and expressed in volume terms. Year-on-year changes are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank data.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details (mth-on-mth)</p>
<p>				   Nov 96   Oct 96   Nov 96 index</p>
<p> Intermediate goods	   -0.8	+2.2	99.4</p>
<p> Capital goods		  +1.9	+4.7     100.7</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables   -0.1	+2.7	88.5</p>
<p> Domestic orders		+1.0	+2.6	88.9</p>
<p> Foreign orders		 -0.8	+3.9     115.4</p>
<p>Two-month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Aug/Sept 96:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +1.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Oct/Nov 95:</p>
<p> Industrial orders		    +6.5</p>
<p> Domestic orders			+2.8</p>
<p> Foreign orders			+13.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		   +7.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			  +7.7</p>
<p> Consumer goods, durables	   +2.2</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097-150</p>
</text>
